0 1 0   1 1 0
b1
;; Adds the two binary numbers specified by initial tape sequence (the first line of this
;; program). Does this by decrementing the second number by one, then incrementing the first
;; number by one, until the second number has been decremented to zero, thus "transferring" all
;; the 1's from the second number to the first. Based on the excellent introduction to Turing
;; Machines published by @samwho: https://samwho.dev/turing-machines/ .
b1 null  R      b2
b1 0     R      b1
b1 1     R      b1
b2 null  L      dec
b2 0     R      b2
b2 1     R      b2
b3 null  L      inc
b3 0     L      b3
b3 1     L      b3
dec null H      dec
dec 0    P:1,L  dec
dec 1    P:0,L  b3
inc null P:1,R  b1
inc 0    P:1,R  b1
inc 1    P:0,L  inc
